{"name":"Rubber","hex":"#815d37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rubber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Pliable material derived from the sap of the rubber tree; a hydrocarbon biopolymer of isoprene.","Natural rubber or any of various synthetic materials with similar properties as natural rubber."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not covered by funds on account."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rubber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Natural rubber","blocks":[{"text":"Rubber, also called India rubber, latex, Amazonian rubber, caucho, or caoutchouc, as initially produced, consists of polymers of the organic compound isoprene, with minor impurities of other organic compounds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Caoutchouc_naturel.jpg/330px-Caoutchouc_naturel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_rubber","wikidata":"Q131877"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Latex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG/500px-Latex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Latex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG/1280px-Latex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Latex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG/500px-Latex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Latex being collected from a tapped rubber tree, Cameroon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALatex_-_Hevea_-_Cameroun.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Rubber_tree_plantation_Thailand_%E3%82%BF%E3%82%A4%E3%81%AE%E3%82%B4%E3%83%A0%E5%9C%92_DSC05246.jpg/500px-Rubber_tree_plantation_Thailand_%E3%82%BF%E3%82%A4%E3%81%AE%E3%82%B4%E3